.TH "POLYGLOT:WORKER" 1 "November 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
polyglot:worker \- Manage hardened, authenticated polyglot persistent workers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php polyglot:worker
\fIaction\fR [\fImodule\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR=\fIlang\fR] [\fB\-\-context\fR=\fIcontext\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B polyglot:worker
orchestrates long-running persistent language workers (Python, Node.js, Perl).
It enforces cryptographically authenticated TCP loopback sockets, non-colliding
atomic PID/port state publication, health check pings, graceful termination,
and automatic stale artifact cleanup.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B start
Spawns the worker daemon, generates auth tokens, and verifies socket readiness.
.TP
.B stop
Sends a graceful shutdown command via the authenticated control channel.
.TP
.B status
Checks whether the worker is alive, queries process metadata, and pings the socket.
.TP
.B restart
Executes a graceful shutdown followed by re-initialization.
.TP
.B cleanup
Scans the daemon registry and purges orphaned PID and port files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR=\fILANGUAGE\fR
Specify the language identifier (python, node, perl).
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR=\fICONTEXT\fR
Application context partition for isolation. Default: default.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
Creates atomic state files under \fIvar/shared/bridge/daemons/\fR.
Validates PID process ownership before termination to prevent PID recycling collisions.
Transports requests with JSON payloads over local loopback sockets with mandatory auth tokens.
